# Mobile vs desktop — keep separate

Two **independent frontends** share only the **same API server** (VPS :8765). They are **not** the same UI with responsive CSS.

| | Desktop | Mobile (SuperNova Short) |
|---|---------|---------------------------|
| Folder | `desktop-ui/` | `mobile-ui/` |
| URL | `/` (root) | `/mobile/` |
| Audience | Full product / power users | **Testers** of the desktop app — simplified companion |
| Layout | Dense dashboards, wide tables, Piggy Bank, Pulse, many panels | **3 tabs:** Dashboard · Portfolio · Opportunities |
| Components | `desktop-ui/src/components/*` | `mobile-ui/src/components/*` only |
| CSS | `desktop-ui/src/index.css`, Tailwind in TSX | `mobile-ui/src/index.css`, `theme.css` |
| Build | `cd desktop-ui && npm run build` | `cd mobile-ui && npm run build` |
| Dev | desktop-ui Vite (port 5173 typical) | `cd mobile-ui && npm run dev` → :5174 |

## Hard rules for agents

1. **Never import** `desktop-ui/` code into `mobile-ui/` (no shared React components).
2. **Never apply** mobile compact styles to desktop (or desktop density to mobile) unless the user **explicitly** names both targets.
3. **Desktop-only changes** (Piggy Bank, Actions table, charts row, panel-stack, simulation grid) → edit **`desktop-ui/` only**.
4. **Mobile-only changes** (OpportunityCard, tab bar, touch forms) → edit **`mobile-ui/` only**.
5. **Shared backend contract** (OK to touch both sides when API changes):
   - `GET/PUT /api/mobile/dashboard-snapshot` — desktop publishes, mobile reads
   - `GET /api/sheets/simulation`, `GET/POST /api/investment/sim-inputs`
   - Types/logic duplicated or mirrored in `mobile-ui/src/` (`simLogic.ts`, `opportunityLogic.ts`) — do not refactor into a shared npm package unless asked.

## Mobile scope (tester MVP)

- Dashboard: KPI preview + few recommendations + links — **not** full desktop dashboard.
- Portfolio: open positions + edit sim (price/capital).
- Opportunities: filtered list/cards + add to simulator.
- Settings sheet: API URL + token only.
- **Out of scope on mobile:** Piggy Bank bar, Pulse table, wide recommendation grid, Model Lab charts, clinical hub, full simulation sheet.

See also: `.cursor/rules/mobile-simplicity.mdc`

## Desktop scope

Full SuperNova desktop — all tabs, dense tables, charts, Decision Lab, etc.

See also: `.cursor/rules/layout-density.mdc` (desktop panels only)

